  "notes": "The Pro HD 24 spec table prints no PoE row: Port Layout \"2.5 GbE RJ45 22 (2.5G/1G/100M/10M), 10 GbE RJ45 2 (10G/5G/2.5G/1G/100M), 10G SFP+ 4 (10G/1G)\", Max. Power Consumption 60W, Power Method \"(1) Universal input, 100-240V AC, 50/60 Hz (1) USP RPS DC input\", internal 60W supply - no per-port wattage and no budget. The PoE member is a separate model with its own budget (usw-pro-hd-24-poe.json), so the absence is a product decision. Without `poeIn: false` its 24 copper sockets each asked for 12.95 W - **310.8 W** of fiction on a box whose whole supply is 60 W."
